Fluid mechanics films and illustrated notes — NCFMF (@fd-films: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_0RT6J26HJJ83MX74030JPEHQVP
National Committee for Fluid Mechanics Films, founded by Ascher Shapiro with the Education Development Center. [Current MIT films and notes entrance](https://hml.mit.edu/ncfmf/).

Watch complete relevant demonstrations and read their notes, beginning with descriptions of motion, deformation, pressure, visualization and low-Reynolds-number flow. Later return to vorticity, boundary layers, interfaces, instability, waves, turbulence, rotation and stratification. Predict what will happen before the demonstration and identify what the images can actually establish.

These are historical educational films with named creators and retained rights, provided for viewing through authorized institutional hosts. The old MIT HML entrance returned 404; the current HML page points to MIT's Office of Digital Learning and film notes. Do not infer a general media-download or adaptation licence from streaming access. All films and notes remain external links.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
